course: dictionary
lesson: 2684
title: Dictator: a ruler, or a bossy person
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A dictator is a ruler who has complete power over a country. Dictators were usually not fairly elected, and they do not allow people to disagree. Read the clues: «Julius Caesar was made dictator of Rome (a leader given total power for a time).» The words total power tell you what kind of power it is.
explain: Clue words point to the same idea. «Cannot be voted out» means the people cannot remove the ruler, and «does not allow people to disagree» means nobody can argue back. Try your meaning in the sentence: a ruler with total power fits; a helper who works in a shop does not.
explain: Dictator also has an informal meaning. «Don't be such a dictator!» is said to someone who tells others what to do and won't listen. Context tells you which meaning is used: is the talk about a country and its freedom, or about a bossy person in a game or at home?
fact: A dictator is a ruler with complete power over a country.
fact: Dictators were usually not fairly elected, and they do not let people disagree.
fact: «Julius Caesar was made dictator of Rome» for a time, but he was never emperor. His adopted son Augustus became the first Roman emperor in 27 BC.
fact: In the 1930s the Great Depression left millions without jobs. In some countries, frightened, angry people turned to dictators who promised strength and blamed others.
fact: Informally, a dictator is someone who tells others what to do and won't listen.
exercise: «Julius Caesar was made dictator of Rome» for a time. What does dictator mean here? | A teacher who gives lots of homework | A person who tells jokes | A soldier who guards a gate | *A leader given total power for a time
exercise: Mum says «Don't be such a dictator!» to Sam, who keeps ordering everyone around. What does dictator mean here? | A kind teacher | A type of bread | A ruler of a country | *Someone who bosses others and won't listen
exercise: A dictator «cannot be voted out». What does this tell you? | They are chosen by children in a school vote | *The people cannot remove them by a vote | Their people are always very happy with them | They lose every election
test: In «Julius Caesar was made dictator of Rome», what does the word tell you about his power? | He had a small job in a shop | He had no power at all | *He had total power, but only for a time | He was a famous poet
test: Which is the best meaning of dictator in «a dictator who won't allow anyone to disagree»? | A kind helper | *A ruler with complete power who does not allow disagreement | A person who draws maps | A famous singer
exam: Which sentence uses dictator in the informal sense? | A dictator cannot be voted out | *«Don't be such a dictator, let us choose the game too!» | In the 1930s, frightened people turned to a dictator who promised strength | Julius Caesar was made dictator of Rome
